\begin{abstract}
We present BasicVSR++, a design that employs a straightforward yet potent framework for video super-resolution (SR). Utilizing a non-recurrent backbone, BasicVSR++ integrates self-similarity matching, optical flow propagation, and other strategies to exploit temporal context. This basic structure supports various video enhancement tasks, such as Super-Resolution (SR), denoising (NR), and combined SR+NR. Our method effectively outperforms state-of-the-art methods on both the RealSR and VID4SR challenges.
